<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shares up on talk of American Air link.</title>
<headline>KLM shares up on talk of American Air link.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in KLM Royal Dutch Airlines were 0.50 firmer at 48.10 guilders at 0955 GMT on Thursday on renewed market speculation of a potential link-up with American Airlines.</p>
<p>Dutch newspaper De Telegraaf quoted American's chairman Bob Crandall as saying he would welcome KLM as a member of its proposed alliance with British Airways.</p>
<p>Dealers said KLM's existing link with Northwest Airlines may block any other deal but added the news was enough to spark interest in the stock in an otherwise quiet market.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
